<%#
# Key figures

One block split by thin vertical dividers (two columns on a phone): a caption, a
big number and an optional note under it. The server-drawn twin of DsStatGroup
(app/javascript/dashboard/components-next/ds/DsStatGroup.vue), so a page drawn by
ERB and a page drawn by Vue show their figures alike.

## Local variables:

- `items`: an array of hashes `{ label:, value:, note: (optional), tone: (optional, :bad) }`.
%>
<dl class="m-0 grid grid-cols-2 overflow-hidden rounded-ds-card border border-solid border-n-weak bg-n-solid-2 md:grid-cols-[repeat(var(--stat-columns),minmax(0,1fr))]" style="--stat-columns: <%= items.size %>">
  <% items.each do |item| %>
    <div class="min-w-0 border-0 border-solid border-n-weak px-5 py-[18px] md:border-e md:last:border-e-0 max-md:odd:border-e max-md:[&:nth-child(n+3)]:border-t" data-testid="stat">
      <dt class="text-ds-caption text-n-slate-11"><%= item[:label] %></dt>
      <dd class="m-0 mt-1.5 truncate text-ds-figure <%= item[:tone] == :bad ? 'text-n-ruby-11' : 'text-n-slate-12' %>"><%= item[:value] %></dd>
      <% if item[:note].present? %>
        <dd class="m-0 mt-1 text-ds-caption text-n-slate-11"><%= item[:note] %></dd>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>
